<title>INDIA: India forex reserves drop to $23.80 bln on Nov 29.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves drop to $23.80 bln on Nov 29.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves fell to $23.80 billion on November 29, 1996, from $23.94 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Nov 29	Nov 22	  Dec 1</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,388	19,532	 17,297</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,382	 4,382	  4,429</p>
<p>    SDRs				    26	    26	     18</p>
<p>    Total			     23,796	23,940	 21,744</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
